  1	#!/usr/bin/env node
  2	// FLEET PANEL — read-mostly web dashboard for the cavecrew bot fleet.
  3	//
  4	// Standalone Node ESM HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:3200. Zero npm deps, Node
  5	// built-ins only. It never touches the runners' internals: it speaks the same
  6	// public HTTP API a driver speaks (see cave/DRIVER_GUIDE.md).
  7	//
  8	// SAFETY CONTRACT — the panel has exactly TWO write actions:
  9	//   POST /api/wake {bot}  -> pushes that bot's role-default task, force:false
 10	//   POST /api/stop {bot}  -> forwards POST /stop to that bot's runner
 11	// force:false is hard-coded and un-overridable, so wake can NEVER preempt a
 12	// driver's running task — a busy runner answers 409 and the panel reports it.
 13	// No RCON, no chat, no world manipulation, no /eval, no other mutations.
 14	//
 15	// This file is the HTTP server + route table ONLY (PANEL V3 SPEC,
 16	// architecture note, phase 1 — the 3-way split). Every parser and every byte
 17	// of data assembly (fleet polling, TODO board, Vault, the two write actions,
 18	// the newer v3 readers) lives in cave/panel-data.mjs, imported below as plain
 19	// named functions — this file never touches a bot's status shape directly.
 20	// The entire client-side script lives in cave/panel-client.js, served
 21	// statically via GET /panel.js rather than inlined into the HTML this file
 22	// renders (kills the double-escaping bug class the architecture note
 23	// describes — see that file's own header for the story).
 24	//
 25	// Docs: cave/PANEL.md
 26	import http from 'node:http';
 27	import fsp from 'node:fs/promises';
 28	import path from 'node:path';
 29	import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
 30	import {
